{"availability":"available","full":"filip26/iridium-cbor-ld","name":"iridium-cbor-ld","description":"Semantic, self-describing binary format for Linked Data","category":"Other","language":"Java","stars":15,"forks":3,"created":"2022-06-30T21:44:21Z","updated":"2026-09-04T08:51:12Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://apicatalog.com","topics":["cbor","cbor-ld","cborld","compression","java","json-ld","linked-data","self-describing","self-descriptive"],"demo":"https://cbor.me/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:59.275Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:59.275Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:59.275Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T11:02:59.275Z","stars":15,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["CBOR-LD is a self-describing binary format that encodes Linked Data expressed in JSON-LD into a compact form. Its primary purpose is to compress the verbose textual representation of JSON-LD into just a few bytes; small enough to embed in a QR code, barcode, or any other constrained medium.","Compression is achieved through semantic compaction by relying on shared semantics. The result can always be expanded back into full JSON-LD without loss of meaning.","The CBOR-LD format makes Linked Data efficient to store, transmit, and embed in environments where space and bandwidth are limited, while retaining semantic interoperability with the wider Linked Data ecosystem."],"features":["🧠 No vibe coding. No generated code. Just deliberate engineering.","🔄 Semantic compression and decompression","⚙️ Configurable API for flexible integration","🧱 Support for custom document dictionaries and builders","📦 Integration with Verifiable Credential Barcodes"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/filip26/iridium-cbor-ld/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"97f1c1675e6f354841075eae082fc4b51c20266f612b30a334a161376358737a","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:59.430Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T11:0